    "generateActionInfo": {
      "impact": "## Impact\nRate impact: 50-90 (low), 100 (normal), 120-150 (high), 150-200 (extreme) based on weapon power and action intensity.",
      "Vanguard Daykeeper Duration": "## VANGUARD DAYKEEPER DURATION\nDo not manually modify `daykeeper.*` or `vga_*` storage through action resolution. Trigger logic owns time and academic state. Explicit durations win. Otherwise treat status checks as 0 minutes; a brief interaction as about 10; nearby movement about 20; focused study/training/repair about 30; meals, dates or substantial meetings about 60. For simultaneous multiplayer actions, shared time advances by the longest parallel action, never by summing all player durations. Formal class completion is recorded by the Academic Ledger, not inferred from elapsed minutes alone.\n\nSpacecraft timing: routine cockpit checks are brief; launch/recovery/docking and meaningful dogfight phases take in-world time; interplanetary/FTL transit follows the established route/drive and explicit duration rather than a generic 20-minute travel assumption. Academic flight practicals still use the Academic Ledger for scheduled-block completion and must not earn duplicate attendance from clock movement.",
      "Clothing, Privacy, and Wardrobe State": "## CLOTHING, PRIVACY, AND WARDROBE STATE\nTreat equipped clothing as current material state. `underwear` is the intimate underlayer; `uniform` is the active outer outfit. Armor/head/weapon/tool slots remain separate. Changing an outer outfit does not strip underwear. Putting armor over a uniform/underlayer does not delete personal clothing unless the story explicitly requires changing or stowing it.\n\nClothing affects what is physically covered, accessible and appropriate to the scene but does not grant hidden social bonuses unless an authored item actually has a mechanical bonus. A glamorous outfit may prompt individual social reactions according to taste, relationship and context; never use it as automatic Persuasion, consent or attraction. Preserve current clothing, removed garments, borrowed garments, damage, wetness and partial redress during a live scene until an action changes them.",
      "V5.12 Action Channels and Progression": "## V5.12 ACTION CHANNELS & PROGRESSION\nKeep difficulty, context modifier, impact, cost and consequence separate. Cover, range, injury, suit condition, equipment, preparation and assistance affect whether/how well an action succeeds; the landed result determines magnitude; consumables/time/resources determine cost; institutional or story state determines consequence.\n\nUse exact structured progression state where available. Attendance counters, qualification traits, resources, skills, level, rank and authored evaluations outrank semantic impressions such as 'seems ready.' A good-looking narration never grants certification by itself. Training or ability breakthroughs require an actual route: instruction, simulator practice, repeated field use, debrief insight, project work, certification, item mastery or another witnessed learning event.",
      "SpaceFleet — Vessel State Handoff": "## SPACEFLEET VESSEL STATE HANDOFF\nTreat exact vessel identity as part of action targeting. Resolve “my ship/current vessel/this craft” to the acting player’s current tracked vessel only when registry context supports it. Boarding does not grant ownership; ownership does not imply presence; fleet command does not erase individual command.\nFor completed travel, distinguish ARRIVED from UNDERWAY. For completed permanent refits, preserve exact installed system and any actually replaced system. For repairs, clear only lasting conditions actually resolved. In spacecraft combat, preserve source, target, range/geometry, readiness, crew presence, installed-system limits, and the host world’s damage model; do not invent universal shields, FTL behavior, weapons, or HP.",
      "SpaceFleet — Docking and Orders": "## SPACEFLEET DOCKING & ORDERS\nTreat carrier docking as an exact child-hull -> carrier-hull relationship. Launch begins at the carrier's current physical position. Do not merge inventories, damage, crew or command between parent and child. Fleet orders are persistent only after valid authority and completed issuance; preserve formation, lead, ROE, rally, escort and standing-order distinctions.",
      "SpaceFleet — Vessel Combat and Operations Fidelity": "## SPACEFLEET ACTION FIDELITY\n- Resolve actions from the exact acting vessel, source system and intended target. Do not transfer another hull's fittings, crew, defenses, readiness or damage onto this action.\n- Separate difficulty, contextual modifiers, impact, cost and consequence. Range, line of sight, firing solution, readiness, power, ammunition/fuel and damaged systems matter only when the host world or current vessel state establishes them.\n- A control/boarding/jamming/towing action is not automatically hull damage. Persistent damage is recorded only when resolved narration establishes a lasting condition on the exact target hull."
