      "beats": "In the Cadet Habitation Ring, formalize the active Flight roster. ALL PCs in the room belong to the same Flight and occupy seats first. Use the nominal six-cadet complement only to determine how many NPC vacancies remain; never split PCs to preserve the number six. Fill vacancies with distinct adult cadets from the authored assignment pool, selecting a varied mix and never duplicating a PC. If six or more PCs are present, the Flight is formally reinforced and needs no filler NPCs. Clearly establish which NPCs, if any, are ACTIVE Flight members; all nonselected candidates belong elsewhere. Once stated, this roster is durable and must not change without an explicit transfer, washout, reassignment, dismissal, death or commission. Keep the scene social and playable: names, room/wing-pair expectations and one immediate point of friction or curiosity. Do not decide attraction or friendship for PCs and do not make everyone speak in a chorus. Completion is reached once the roster is understood and players have had a chance to respond.",
      "targetTurns": 2,
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "quest-objective-complete",
          "questId": "Orientation Week",
          "objectiveId": "meet_flight"
        },
        {
          "type": "quest-objective-reveal",
          "questId": "Orientation Week",
          "objectiveId": "check_terminal"
        },
        {
          "type": "quest-next-step-set",
          "questId": "Orientation Week",
          "text": "Check the Cadet Terminal for today's schedule and your Academic Ledger.",
          "source": "narrative-event"
        }
      ]
    },
    "Empty Berths": {
      "title": "The Empty Berths",
      "beats": "The Flight returns to the habitation ring and finds several senior residential clusters abruptly cleared. No attack occurs here. Orders moved those cadets to provisional commissions overnight. An instructor is also absent. Let the emptiness, administrative notices and reactions carry the scene. Do not force a speech. Completion occurs when the players understand that the academy is being consumed by mobilization.",
      "targetTurns": 2,
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "After this event, treat accelerated commissioning and instructor recalls as established background pressure, but do not interrupt unrelated quiet scenes without cause."
        }
      ]
    },
    "Basic Flight Check Ride": {
      "title": "Basic Flight Check Ride",
      "beats": "Commander Seraphine Kade, or the ledger-authorized substitute if Kade is unavailable, conducts the final supervised basic flight check. Use the player's actual Piloting, Astrogation, judgement and current craft state. Include at least one emergency or imperfect-information decision. Do not auto-pass because the event started. Completion means the evaluator has reached and stated a formal pass/fail decision. If the story establishes failure, stop without pretending qualification was earned.",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "quest-complete",
          "questId": "Earn Your Wings"
        },
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "This evaluation has concluded. Preserve each individual cadet’s explicitly stated pass/fail result. Completion of the event itself does not grant the qualification trait."
        }
      ]
    },
    "Basic Field Evaluation": {
      "title": "Basic Field Evaluation",
      "beats": "Major Raxa Venn conducts or supervises a combined boarding-and-ground evaluation using the Resolute hulk. Test tactical planning, movement, target discrimination, EVA/boarding discipline and the ability to continue after a plan changes. Do not auto-pass because the event started. Completion means an evaluator has stated a formal pass/fail decision.",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "quest-complete",
          "questId": "Ground Side"
        },
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "This evaluation has concluded. Preserve each individual cadet’s explicitly stated pass/fail result. Completion of the event itself does not grant the qualification trait."
        }
      ]
    },
    "Basic Technical Evaluation": {
      "title": "Basic Technical Evaluation",
      "beats": "Chief Vora Sen and Dr. Asha Ren supervise a combined damage-control and casualty-support scenario. Give individual cadets distinct jobs. Test safe power isolation, repair priorities, triage support, communication and adaptation when equipment fails. The event can contain individual passes and failures within the same Flight. Completion occurs once evaluators have stated results; do not mechanically grant qualification merely because the event completed.",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "quest-complete",
          "questId": "Keep It Running"
        },
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "The technical evaluation has concluded. Preserve each individual cadet’s stated pass/fail result; failed cadets require remediation and are not qualified."
        }
      ]
    },
    "Basic Command Board": {
      "title": "Basic Command Board",
      "beats": "Colonel Marcus Okafor runs a junior-command board built around an ambiguous mixed-species operational problem. Test intent, delegation, legal authority, cross-species judgement, willingness to revise a plan and the ability to distinguish command from control. Each PC receives an individual result even though the Flight may attend together. Completion occurs once formal results are stated; do not auto-pass everyone.",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "quest-complete",
          "questId": "Command Under Pressure"
        },
        {
          "type": "story",
          "instruction": "The command board has concluded. Preserve individual pass/fail results and schedule remediation for failures."
        }
      ]
    },
    "Zero-G Games": {
      "title": "Zero-G Games Night",
      "beats": "An optional evening of inter-Flight zero-g athletics, informal competition and socializing in the Zero-G Athletics Hall. Use Aster, Manticore and Halcyon cadets when useful. Let sport create rivalry, attraction, embarrassment or friendship without manufacturing danger. Participation is voluntary and losing is not academic failure.",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "onCompleteEffects": [
        {
          "type": "player-resource",
          "resource": "Flight Cohesion",
          "operator": "add",
          "value": 3,
          "target": "allPlayers"
        }
      ]
    },
    "Concord Culture Night": {
      "title": "Concord Culture Night",
      "beats": "An optional Cultural Exchange Hall event where cadets and visiting personnel share food, music, games, clothing traditions, stories and arguments. Do not reduce species to one custom each. Queer, polyamorous and cross-species relationships can be ordinary parts of the crowd without becoming the event’s sole subject. Keep it social unless an established cause intrudes.",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "onCompleteEffects": []
    },
    "Founders Mess": {
      "title": "Founders’ Mess",
      "beats": "A formal but lively Vanguard mess night before mobilization fully changes academy life. Flights wear dress uniforms, instructors circulate, rivalries and romances have room to breathe, and speeches remain short. The event should reflect the current war stage in background details without hijacking the evening with an unrelated emergency.",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "onCompleteEffects": []
    },
    "Interflight Games": {
      "title": "Interflight Games Weekend",
      "beats": "A voluntary inter-Flight competition across simulator flying, zero-g movement, tactical problem solving and practical teamwork. Use Aster, Manticore, Halcyon and the player Flight as peers rather than enemies. Only PCs whose actions establish attendance are present; never teleport split multiplayer PCs into the event. Winning, losing, spectating, helping, flirting, leaving early or ignoring an event are all legitimate. No sabotage is required.",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "onCompleteEffects": []
    },
    "Vanguard Formal": {
      "title": "Vanguard Formal",
      "beats": "An adult academy formal with dress uniforms, personal fashion, music, food, dancing, friends, dates, instructors and visiting personnel. Attendance is voluntary; a date is not required; attraction and consent remain separate. Only PCs actually established at the formal are present. Let the current war stage color the room without manufacturing an emergency.",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "onCompleteEffects": []
    },
    "Posting and Career Fair": {
      "title": "Posting and Career Fair",
      "beats": "A practical academy event where branches, fleets, expeditionary units, research services and liaison programs explain real paths after qualification. Invitations and recruiter interest are not offers of rank or guaranteed posting. Only participating PCs are present. Let interests, records, reputation and questions matter without forcing a career decision.",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "onCompleteEffects": []
    },
    "Exchange Showcase": {
      "title": "Concord Exchange Showcase",
      "beats": "A mixed-species showcase of training, culture, technology and public-facing academy work. Keep species cultures internally varied. Participation can be presentation, performance, demonstration, volunteering, watching or leaving. If mobilization has cancelled the showcase, this event must not start.",
      "targetTurns": 3,
      "onCompleteEffects": []
    }
  },
